Subject: [PATCH 5/5] P8: CGS channels take their vendor's request style

The CGS channels speak their vendor's own wire, but omp keys vendor rules on
the provider id, so cgs-antigravity and cgs-codex fell back to the generic
wire of their api:

- cgs-antigravity resolves under google-antigravity's rules (Gemini needs the
  skip-thought-signature sentinel on the first function call) and runs the
  Antigravity request path: envelope, VALIDATED tool mode, client headers.
  The updater-manifest lookup stays with the official provider so a relay-bound
  channel does not reach past its gateway.
- cgs-codex borrows only apply-patch-tool-type from openai-codex: the freeform
  apply_patch tool. Codex's dollar prices and windows are not taken.
- cgs-claude already gets Claude Code's shape from its api; cgs-openai
  (deepseek and others) has no vendor style.
